210
00:10:03,810 --> 00:10:06,630
But about Playlab, for those of you that might not born,

211
00:10:06,630 --> 00:10:10,623
it was born in 2022, it was actually,

212
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:13,590
there was a product that was for the team,

213
00:10:13,590 --> 00:10:16,030
the founding team, they made something on GPT 3

214
00:10:17,490 --> 00:10:21,570
that was founded by Google and that achieved acquisition.

215
00:10:21,570 --> 00:10:23,490
But the team started to notice

216
00:10:23,490 --> 00:10:26,250
that despite the success in these commercial AI

217
00:10:26,250 --> 00:10:27,720
and research applications

218
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:29,807
that they were doing at MIT,

219
00:10:29,807 --> 00:10:31,500
educators weren't really using them.

220
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:33,660
So that's when Playlab was founded

221
00:10:33,660 --> 00:10:34,980
because it was this notion

222
00:10:34,980 --> 00:10:39,120
that educators shouldn't be passed down ed tech tools

223
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:41,970
and not have a say in sort of determining like

224
00:10:41,970 --> 00:10:44,040
what do these tools do for us,

225
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:45,060
but be creators

226
00:10:45,060 --> 00:10:48,030
of these tools rather than just passive recipients.

227
00:10:48,030 --> 00:10:51,780
So what happened was when they sort

228
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:54,420
of gave educators the tools in terms of being able

229
00:10:54,420 --> 00:10:56,130
to build their own chatbots

230
00:10:56,130 --> 00:10:57,390
or own AI tools in order

231
00:10:57,390 --> 00:11:00,000
to solve problems in specific contexts,

232
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,730
that these were really powerful things

233
00:11:02,730 --> 00:11:05,430
that educators were building to solve these problems.

234
00:11:05,430 --> 00:11:09,930
And they were really cracking like the nut, you could say,

235
00:11:09,930 --> 00:11:13,140
of how do we solve like some wicked problems

236
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:14,310
in the classroom,

237
00:11:14,310 --> 00:11:17,070
not all the way, but really starting to make some headway

238
00:11:17,070 --> 00:11:18,630
and how can you use this application

239
00:11:18,630 --> 00:11:20,010
in these particular ways.

240
00:11:20,010 --> 00:11:22,800
So it really created some fundamental shifts around

241
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:25,620
how teaching and learning has started to happen.

242
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:27,670
And we're seeing that a lot with Playlab.

243
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:32,340
So the thing that also is really important

244
00:11:32,340 --> 00:11:35,430
to know about Playlab is it's a non-profit organization.

245
00:11:35,430 --> 00:11:37,040
And one of the reasons

246
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:40,260
that Playlab is a non-profit organization is

247
00:11:40,260 --> 00:11:43,440
because we're really mindful, very thoughtful about

248
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:45,940
how do we protect our young people

249
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:50,100
and protect really what's the responsibility, right,

250
00:11:50,100 --> 00:11:53,010
of like this technology is very disruptive

251
00:11:53,010 --> 00:11:55,920
and how do we support our educators in being able

252
00:11:55,920 --> 00:12:00,420
to manage it, to think about how to integrate it.

253
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:03,420
And so one of the things was like, hey,

254
00:12:03,420 --> 00:12:04,680
our systems are already,

255
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:07,143
like pedagogy as an educator,

256
00:12:08,190 --> 00:12:10,140
it's already kind of broken, right?

257
00:12:10,140 --> 00:12:11,987
The systems are already hard.

258
00:12:11,987 --> 00:12:16,080
Education is, there's already systems in place

259
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:18,210
that aren't always serving students

260
00:12:18,210 --> 00:12:22,440
and AI can, unfortunately, just kind of reinforce that

261
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:24,090
and exacerbate it further.

262
00:12:24,090 --> 00:12:27,000
So premature scaling is really not something

263
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,233
we wanted to do.

264
00:12:29,433 --> 00:12:30,266
If you do so,

